findings.problem:
`isCyclic_of_spe` repeats the proof of `isCyclic_of_isPGroup_three` in OddIndex/ReductionGroup.lean. Both do the same steps:
- get a Sylow P inside N from `exists_sylow_le_of_glbStronglyEmbedded`;
- conjugate R into P with `MulAction.exists_smul_eq`;
- run the same `hle` argument with `smul_mem_pointwise_smul`;
- apply `isCyclic_of_pRank_le_one`;
- transfer cyclicity back along `equivMapOfInjective`.
The only differences are the hypothesis form (`GLBStronglyEmbedded` against `IsStronglyPEmbedded`, which `glb_of_spe` already converts) and `pRank ≤ 1` against `pRank = 1`. Even the `pRank` bridge in lines 36-40 re-inlines the body of `pRank_le_one_of_open_eq_one`, which only uses `h1.le`. The ~25-line Sylow-conjugation argument is therefore maintained in two places, and a change to one will not reach the other.
